      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sharon%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community was originally settled as Hackberry on Persimmon Creek following the 1893 Cherokee Outlet land opening.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sharon_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Sharon relocated five miles northwest in 1912 to align with the Wichita Falls and Northwestern Railway.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.okhistory.org/publications/enc/entry?entry=SH008"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A coin toss between two families who owned the town site determined that the community would be named Sharon.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
